cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  prismabib: a reproducible PRISMA and bibliometric research pipeline
message: >-
  If you use prismabib to produce numbers reported in a publication, please
  cite it, and cite the exact release you ran. Every number this tool emits is
  traceable to a Layer 0 capture and a package version; a citation without a
  version cannot be checked by a reader.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Huesca
    given-names: Sergio
repository-code: "https://github.com/SergioHuesca/PRISMA-Bib"
url: "https://sergiohuesca.github.io/PRISMA-Bib/"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for executing a PRISMA 2020 systematic review over Scopus
  with reproducible, auditable numbers. Raw API responses are persisted
  verbatim and sealed; the analytical store is rebuildable from them by one
  function call; screening decisions are an append-only, checksummed event log
  that can be replayed under amended eligibility criteria; and every reported
  count is a query against that store rather than a literal typed into prose.
keywords:
  - systematic-review
  - PRISMA
  - bibliometrics
  - reproducible-research
  - scopus
  - meta-research
license: MIT
